.kt-card-header
  %h3.kt-card-title
    Team
.kt-card-content
  %p.text-sm.text-foreground-secondary
    The Team is created at the Account level to centralize your collaborators. Its power lies in its flexibility: you assign custom rights at the Organization, Project or Workspace level to ensure maximum security.

  %h4.mb-2.mt-4 Centralized creation (Account Level):
  %p.text-sm.text-foreground-secondary
    All teams are created and managed at the global Account level. This is where you manage members and the team identity. A team created once can then be used anywhere across the organization.
    %h4.mb-2.mt-4 Flexible rights assignment:
  %p.text-sm.text-foreground-secondary.mb-4
    Once the team is created, you can grant specific permissions ("Read only", "Edit", "Admin") across the three lower levels, according to your needs:
  %p.text-sm.text-foreground-secondary.mb-4
    At the
    %b Organization
    level:
    To grant access to all projects within a subsidiary or department.
  %p.text-sm.text-foreground-secondary.mb-4
    At the
    %b Project
    level:
    To restrict access to a specific product or application (including environment definitions).
  %p.text-sm.text-foreground-secondary.mb-4
    At the
    %b Workspace
    level:
    For granular control, allowing for example a team to modify the Key/Values or Terraform files of a "Dev" environment without touching "Prod".
